hermes v2026.9.14 (0.21.3): every gateway shutdown broadcasts
"⚠️ Gateway shutting down — Your current task will be interrupted." to
each platform's home channel, whether or not any session is running.
Where every deploy restarts all native agents, each user's home chat
gets the notice on every deploy (two deploys in one evening: nine
home-channel sends, all with active_at_start=0).

The per-session notice to chats with a running agent stays; those
sessions are marked resume_pending and auto-continue on the next boot.
A chat without a running agent loses nothing to a restart, so the
home-channel broadcast goes. The drain marker's suppress_notification
flag only ever gated that broadcast and is now inert.

The two tests that pinned the broadcast become its negation: no session
-> nothing sent (restart and shutdown), and an active session is pinged
while the home channel is not. Both fail without this change.

